  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 347 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nThe summertime upper level ridge of high pressure will continue to\nreside over the Great Basin for a few more days, before gradually\nbreaking down a bit by the middle of next week. Afternoon\ntemperatures will be on the warm side today, but I did lower the\nvalleys of Southwest MT today a few degrees below guidance, with\nthe thick smoke, afternoon temperatures are not getting quite as\nwarm as models prog. Otherwise, there is about a 10 percent chance\nfor a dry thunderstorm near the MT/ID border west of Monida Pass\ntowards evening. Expect a wind shift over North Central MT around\nmid day, this will keep afternoon temperatures just a bit lower\nover the north today as well.\n\nFor Sunday through Tuesday, a very gradual and slow cooling trend\nis expected, along with mostly dry conditions.\n\nFor Wednesday through Saturday, an upper level trof of low\npressure is expected to move southward into the northern portions\nof MT by Thursday. This will result in quite a bit cooler\ntemperatures, especially over the northern portions of the CWA.\nToday, the 00z run of the GFS is about 30 degrees colder with\nafternoon temperatures than yesterday's 00z run over North \nCentral MT. Over Southwest MT, it should turn cooler, just not as\ncool as North Central MT. Additionally, the GFS/EC are averaging \nbetween 0.10 and 0.20 inches of precipitation over North Central \nMT from Wed into Thu. This isn't a lot of precipitation, but more\nthan what has fallen recently. The upper level trof could exit \nthe area by next Saturday, resulting in an unstable southwesterly \nflow aloft setting up.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nWith the 00z GFS today progging temperatures about 30 degrees\ncolder than yesterday over North Central MT by next Thursday, \nconfidence is a bit uncertain about the timing/strength of the \ncolder air by the middle of next week. Additionally, how far south\ndoes the precipitation go before cutting off. Brusda",
